{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-22354","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22272","text":"Dual- and Triple-Loop Machine Architecture"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22273","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE update (OS-010, 2026-04):"},{"id":"spn-22274","text":" With the introduction of OS-010 PULSE, the loop-interlock pattern documented here is now formalized as a manifest standard. Graphonomous, PRISM, AgenTroMatic, and every other portfolio loop declare their phases in "},{"id":"spn-22275","marks":["code"],"text":"<loop>.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-22276","text":" files (see "},{"id":"spn-22277","marks":["code"],"text":"/PULSE/manifests/"},{"id":"spn-22278","text":"), validated against "},{"id":"spn-22279","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-22280","text":". The \"dual loop\" is a special case of arbitrarily nestable PULSE loops — the same machine grouping works at any depth, and PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-22281","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-22282","text":" phase reads the inner system's PULSE manifest to discover the "},{"id":"spn-22283","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-22284","text":" boundary at runtime rather than hard-coding the integration. See \"Triple loop and beyond\" below."}]}],"id":"blk-22355","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-22357","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22285","text":"Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-22358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22286","text":"PRISM and Graphonomous are both closed-loop systems. When PRISM evaluates Graphonomous, their loops interlock — the outer loop (PRISM) improves the benchmark while the inner loop (Graphonomous) improves the memory. Each makes the other sharper."}]},{"id":"blk-22359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22287","text":"The machine architecture solves the tool explosion problem: 47 PRISM tools + 29 Graphonomous tools = 76 tools in a shared session. Research shows tool selection accuracy degrades to ~49% at that scale, and schema overhead burns 40-80K tokens."}]},{"id":"blk-22360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22288","marks":["bold"],"text":"Solution:"},{"id":"spn-22289","text":" Group tools by loop phase, not category. 6 PRISM machines + 5 Graphonomous machines = 11 tools. Selection accuracy jumps to ~95%."}]},{"id":"blk-22361","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22290","text":"The Interlocking Loops"}]},{"id":"blk-22362","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Graphonomous (memory loop)          PRISM (evaluation loop)\n──────────────────────────          ───────────────────────\nretrieve  \"What do I know?\"         compose    \"What should I test?\"\nroute     \"What should I do?\"       interact   \"Run the test\"\nact       \"Do it\"                   observe    \"Judge the result\"\nlearn     \"Did it work?\"            reflect    \"What should change?\"\nconsolidate \"Clean up\"              diagnose   \"What's actionable?\""},{"id":"blk-22363","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22291","text":"When PRISM benchmarks Graphonomous:"}]},{"id":"blk-22364","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"PRISM compose ──→ PRISM interact ──→ PRISM observe ──→ PRISM reflect ──→ PRISM diagnose\n                       │\n                       ▼\n              ┌─── Graphonomous ───┐\n              │  retrieve → route  │\n              │  → act → learn     │\n              │  → consolidate     │\n              └────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-22365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22292","text":"PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-22293","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-22294","text":" phase drives the system-under-test through its own closed loop. PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-22295","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-22296","text":" phase judges how well that inner loop performed. PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-22297","marks":["code"],"text":"reflect"},{"id":"spn-22298","text":" phase evolves scenarios based on where the inner loop failed."}]},{"id":"blk-22366","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22299","text":"PRISM: 47 tools → 6 machines"}]},{"id":"blk-22367","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22300","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-22301","text":" — \"What should I test?\" (9 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22302","marks":["code"],"text":"scenarios"},{"id":"spn-22303","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22304","marks":["code"],"text":"validate"},{"id":"spn-22305","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22306","marks":["code"],"text":"list"},{"id":"spn-22307","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22308","marks":["code"],"text":"get"},{"id":"spn-22309","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22310","marks":["code"],"text":"retire"},{"id":"spn-22311","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22312","marks":["code"],"text":"import"},{"id":"spn-22313","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22314","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_register"},{"id":"spn-22315","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22316","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_discover"},{"id":"spn-22317","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22318","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_generate"}]},{"id":"blk-22369","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22319","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-22320","text":" — \"Run the test\" (8 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22321","marks":["code"],"text":"run"},{"id":"spn-22322","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22323","marks":["code"],"text":"run_sequence"},{"id":"spn-22324","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22325","marks":["code"],"text":"run_matrix"},{"id":"spn-22326","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22327","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-22328","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22329","marks":["code"],"text":"transcript"},{"id":"spn-22330","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22331","marks":["code"],"text":"cancel"},{"id":"spn-22332","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22333","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_evaluate"},{"id":"spn-22334","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22335","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_compare"}]},{"id":"blk-22371","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22336","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-22337","text":" — \"Judge the result\" (5 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22338","marks":["code"],"text":"judge_transcript"},{"id":"spn-22339","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22340","marks":["code"],"text":"judge_dimension"},{"id":"spn-22341","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22342","marks":["code"],"text":"meta_judge"},{"id":"spn-22343","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22344","marks":["code"],"text":"meta_judge_batch"},{"id":"spn-22345","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22346","marks":["code"],"text":"override"}]},{"id":"blk-22373","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22347","marks":["code"],"text":"reflect"},{"id":"spn-22348","text":" — \"What should change?\" (7 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22349","marks":["code"],"text":"analyze_gaps"},{"id":"spn-22350","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22351","marks":["code"],"text":"evolve"},{"id":"spn-22352","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22353","marks":["code"],"text":"advance_cycle"},{"id":"spn-22354","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22355","marks":["code"],"text":"calibrate_irt"},{"id":"spn-22356","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22357","marks":["code"],"text":"cycle_history"},{"id":"spn-22358","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22359","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_recommend"},{"id":"spn-22360","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22361","marks":["code"],"text":"byor_infer_profile"}]},{"id":"blk-22375","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22362","marks":["code"],"text":"diagnose"},{"id":"spn-22363","text":" — \"What's actionable?\" (13 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22364","marks":["code"],"text":"report"},{"id":"spn-22365","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22366","marks":["code"],"text":"failure_patterns"},{"id":"spn-22367","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22368","marks":["code"],"text":"retest"},{"id":"spn-22369","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22370","marks":["code"],"text":"verify"},{"id":"spn-22371","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22372","marks":["code"],"text":"regressions"},{"id":"spn-22373","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22374","marks":["code"],"text":"suggest_fixes"},{"id":"spn-22375","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22376","marks":["code"],"text":"leaderboard"},{"id":"spn-22377","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22378","marks":["code"],"text":"leaderboard_history"},{"id":"spn-22379","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22380","marks":["code"],"text":"compare_systems"},{"id":"spn-22381","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22382","marks":["code"],"text":"dimension_leaders"},{"id":"spn-22383","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22384","marks":["code"],"text":"fit_recommendation"},{"id":"spn-22385","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22386","marks":["code"],"text":"compare_fit"},{"id":"spn-22387","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22388","marks":["code"],"text":"task_profiles"}]},{"id":"blk-22377","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22389","marks":["code"],"text":"config"},{"id":"spn-22390","text":" — Admin/setup (5 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22391","marks":["code"],"text":"set_weights"},{"id":"spn-22392","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22393","marks":["code"],"text":"register_system"},{"id":"spn-22394","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22395","marks":["code"],"text":"list_systems"},{"id":"spn-22396","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22397","marks":["code"],"text":"get_config"},{"id":"spn-22398","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22399","marks":["code"],"text":"create_profile"}]},{"id":"blk-22379","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22400","text":"Graphonomous: 29 tools → 5 machines"}]},{"id":"blk-22380","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22401","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-22402","text":" — \"What do I know?\" (6 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22381","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22403","marks":["code"],"text":"context"},{"id":"spn-22404","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22405","marks":["code"],"text":"episodic"},{"id":"spn-22406","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22407","marks":["code"],"text":"procedural"},{"id":"spn-22408","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22409","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage"},{"id":"spn-22410","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22411","marks":["code"],"text":"trace_evidence"},{"id":"spn-22412","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22413","marks":["code"],"text":"frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-22382","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22414","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-22415","text":" — \"What should I do?\" (5 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22383","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22416","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"},{"id":"spn-22417","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22418","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"},{"id":"spn-22419","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22420","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"},{"id":"spn-22421","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22422","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_cycle"},{"id":"spn-22423","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22424","marks":["code"],"text":"review_goal"}]},{"id":"blk-22384","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22425","marks":["code"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-22426","text":" — \"Do it\" (9 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22427","marks":["code"],"text":"store_node"},{"id":"spn-22428","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22429","marks":["code"],"text":"store_edge"},{"id":"spn-22430","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22431","marks":["code"],"text":"delete_node"},{"id":"spn-22432","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22433","marks":["code"],"text":"manage_edge"},{"id":"spn-22434","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22435","marks":["code"],"text":"manage_goal"},{"id":"spn-22436","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22437","marks":["code"],"text":"belief_revise"},{"id":"spn-22438","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22439","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_node"},{"id":"spn-22440","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22441","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_policy"},{"id":"spn-22442","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22443","marks":["code"],"text":"gdpr_erase"}]},{"id":"blk-22386","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22444","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-22445","text":" — \"Did it work?\" (5 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22446","marks":["code"],"text":"from_outcome"},{"id":"spn-22447","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22448","marks":["code"],"text":"from_feedback"},{"id":"spn-22449","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22450","marks":["code"],"text":"detect_novelty"},{"id":"spn-22451","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22452","marks":["code"],"text":"from_interaction"},{"id":"spn-22453","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22454","marks":["code"],"text":"contradictions"}]},{"id":"blk-22388","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22455","marks":["code"],"text":"consolidate"},{"id":"spn-22456","text":" — \"Clean up\" (4 actions)"}]},{"id":"blk-22389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22457","marks":["code"],"text":"run"},{"id":"spn-22458","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22459","marks":["code"],"text":"stats"},{"id":"spn-22460","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22461","marks":["code"],"text":"query"},{"id":"spn-22462","text":", "},{"id":"spn-22463","marks":["code"],"text":"traverse"}]},{"id":"blk-22390","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22464","text":"Combined Impact"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-22392","spans":[{"id":"spn-22465","text":"Scenario"}]},{"id":"blk-22393","spans":[{"id":"spn-22466","text":"Before"}]},{"id":"blk-22394","spans":[{"id":"spn-22467","text":"After"}]}],"id":"blk-22391","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-22395","spans":[{"id":"spn-22468","text":"Graphonomous alone"}]},{"id":"blk-22396","spans":[{"id":"spn-22469","text":"29 tools"}]},{"id":"blk-22397","spans":[{"id":"spn-22470","text":"5 tools"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22398","spans":[{"id":"spn-22471","text":"PRISM alone"}]},{"id":"blk-22399","spans":[{"id":"spn-22472","text":"47 tools"}]},{"id":"blk-22400","spans":[{"id":"spn-22473","text":"6 tools"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22401","spans":[{"id":"spn-22474","text":"Both in same session"}]},{"id":"blk-22402","spans":[{"id":"spn-22475","text":"76 tools"}]},{"id":"blk-22403","spans":[{"id":"spn-22476","text":"11 tools"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-22404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22477","text":"Context savings: ~85% reduction in tool schema tokens. Selection accuracy: from ~49% (76 tools) to ~95% (11 tools)."}]},{"id":"blk-22405","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22478","text":"Implementation"}]},{"id":"blk-22406","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22479","text":"Both systems use the same Elixir pattern: a single Anubis.Server.Component module per machine with an "},{"id":"spn-22480","marks":["code"],"text":"action"},{"id":"spn-22481","text":" field that dispatches internally to the existing tool implementations. The v1 tool modules are preserved as the implementation layer."}]},{"id":"blk-22407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22482","text":"See:"}]},{"id":"blk-22408","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22410","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22483","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/lib/graphonomous/mcp/machines/"},{"id":"spn-22484","text":" — Graphonomous machine modules"}]}],"id":"blk-22409","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22412","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22485","marks":["code"],"text":"PRISM/lib/prism/mcp/machines/"},{"id":"spn-22486","text":" — PRISM machine modules"}]}],"id":"blk-22411","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22414","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22487","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/prompts/DUAL_LOOP_MACHINES.md"},{"id":"spn-22488","text":" — canonical architecture design"}]}],"id":"blk-22413","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22415","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22489","text":"Triple loop and beyond — PULSE generalization"}]},{"id":"blk-22416","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22490","text":"The Graphonomous ↔ PRISM dual loop is the canonical example, but the [&] ecosystem actually runs "},{"id":"spn-22491","marks":["bold"],"text":"at least three"},{"id":"spn-22492","text":" nested loops today:"}]},{"id":"blk-22417","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"PRISM (outer)        compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose\n  │\n  └─ Graphonomous    retrieve → route → act → learn → consolidate\n       │\n       └─ Deliberation    survey → triage → dispatch → act → learn"},{"id":"blk-22418","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22493","text":"OS-010 PULSE encodes this nesting in each manifest's "},{"id":"spn-22494","marks":["code"],"text":"nesting"},{"id":"spn-22495","text":" block:"}]},{"id":"blk-22419","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22421","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22496","marks":["code"],"text":"prism.benchmark"},{"id":"spn-22497","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-22498","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.continual_learning]"}]}],"id":"blk-22420","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22499","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.continual_learning"},{"id":"spn-22500","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-22501","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [graphonomous.deliberate]"},{"id":"spn-22502","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-22503","marks":["code"],"text":"parent_loop: prism.benchmark"}]}],"id":"blk-22422","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-22425","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22504","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.deliberate"},{"id":"spn-22505","text":" declares "},{"id":"spn-22506","marks":["code"],"text":"parent_loop: graphonomous.continual_learning"}]}],"id":"blk-22424","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-22426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22507","text":"PULSE supports unbounded nesting depth. OS-008 (Agent Harness, draft) is expected to add a fourth outer layer that wraps PRISM itself — when it ships, the only change required is a new manifest with "},{"id":"spn-22508","marks":["code"],"text":"inner_loops: [prism.benchmark]"},{"id":"spn-22509","text":". No code changes to existing machines."}]},{"id":"blk-22427","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22510","text":"Why this matters for the machine architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-22428","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22511","text":"The 5/6/11-tool count documented above is a "},{"id":"spn-22512","marks":["bold"],"text":"floor"},{"id":"spn-22513","text":", not a ceiling. Adding a third loop adds at most 5 more machines (one per phase kind), and because PULSE manifests declare the inner-loop boundary explicitly, the outer machines do not need to learn about inner machines individually. PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-22514","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-22515","text":" machine, for example, drives any PULSE-conforming inner loop through its declared "},{"id":"spn-22516","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-22517","text":" phase — it does not need a Graphonomous-specific code path."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-22430","spans":[{"id":"spn-22518","text":"Layers in session"}]},{"id":"blk-22431","spans":[{"id":"spn-22519","text":"Tool count (machines)"}]},{"id":"blk-22432","spans":[{"id":"spn-22520","text":"Tool count (legacy v1)"}]}],"id":"blk-22429","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-22433","spans":[{"id":"spn-22521","text":"Graphonomous alone"}]},{"id":"blk-22434","spans":[{"id":"spn-22522","text":"5"}]},{"id":"blk-22435","spans":[{"id":"spn-22523","text":"29"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22436","spans":[{"id":"spn-22524","text":"Graphonomous + PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-22437","spans":[{"id":"spn-22525","text":"11"}]},{"id":"blk-22438","spans":[{"id":"spn-22526","text":"76"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22439","spans":[{"id":"spn-22527","text":"Graphonomous + PRISM + OS-008 Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-22440","spans":[{"id":"spn-22528","text":"~16"}]},{"id":"blk-22441","spans":[{"id":"spn-22529","text":"~100+"}]}],[{"id":"blk-22442","spans":[{"id":"spn-22530","text":"Graphonomous + PRISM + OS-008 + AgenTroMatic deliberation"}]},{"id":"blk-22443","spans":[{"id":"spn-22531","text":"~21"}]},{"id":"blk-22444","spans":[{"id":"spn-22532","text":"~130+"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-22445","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22533","text":"The savings compound with depth, and PULSE's manifest standard is what makes the composition algebraic instead of ad-hoc."}]},{"id":"blk-22446","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-22534","text":"Three-protocol stack at runtime"}]},{"id":"blk-22447","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM    — measures loops over time      (diagnostic)   │ OS-009\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE    — declares loops + circulation   (temporal)    │ OS-010\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&]      — composes capabilities          (structural)  │ AmpersandBoxDesign\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-22448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-22535","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-22536","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-22537","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-22538","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-22539","text":" and its runtime passes all 12 conformance tests. A system is "},{"id":"spn-22540","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-22541","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-22542","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-22543","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-22544","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-22545","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-22546","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-22547","text":" phase. No bespoke per-system integration required."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieral2ri5m2mtbzgrov2ttjbc2swjz4eb4sl7wpzc62uo2lohqnathkq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}